+	 * and no device on the system was classified as a tablet.  libinput
+	 * decides what a device *is* from its capability bitmap, not from the
+	 * events it emits: 0051..0066 have been reporting ABS_MT_TOOL_TYPE =
+	 * MT_TOOL_PEN on every stroke (verified 100% of contacts), yet without
+	 * BTN_TOOL_PEN in evdev::key libinput classified the whole thing as a
+	 * touch screen and the compositors therefore ran every pen stroke
+	 * through the pointer path.
+	 *
+	 * The symptom was specific and reproducible: free-hand strokes and
+	 * handwriting were smooth, while *drag-select* operations -- dragging
+	 * an icon, dragging across text to select it -- visibly shook, because
+	 * those take an exclusive grab and the compositor/applies its own
+	 * pointer handling.  Same coordinate stream, different consumer.
+	 *
+	 * This is the same contract wacom_setup_pen_input_capabilities() sets
