+	 *
+	 * BTN_TOOL_PEN means "the pen is in range" and is a *pair* key, unlike
+	 * BTN_TOUCH ("the tip is down").  himax_report_tracked_state() keeps
+	 * the two in step: BTN_TOOL_PEN is raised with the first pen slot and
+	 * dropped together with the ABS_MT_TOOL_TYPE = MT_TOOL_FINGER that 0066
+	 * already writes on pen-up, so libinput never sees a pen that never
+	 * leaves range.  BTN_TOOL_RUBBER is the eraser on this digitiser, and
+	 * BTN_STYLUS the barrel button -- neither exists here, so neither is
+	 * declared.
+	 */
+	/*
+	 * ROLLED BACK 2026-10-04 23:0x -- see below.
+	 * Declaring BTN_TOOL_PEN flips libinput from "touch" to "tablet"
+	 * (verified: `libinput list-devices` Capabilities: touch -> tablet),
+	 * but with the axis resolutions this driver reports it then sizes the
